    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can you dig a bit deeper into the bitumen side of things? specifically how the viscosity changes during those extreme phoenix temp swings and if that's affecting the binder's ability to handle the stress. also, could there be an issue with the subgrade compaction contributing to it?",
